  "verdict": "Walk-forward backtest, 2012-2021 (22,765 games, prediction before update, lines never used as inputs): the team-level runs model picks the winner 55.6% straight up. Brier score 0.2444 vs 0.2402 for the vig-removed closing line -- the line remains the sharper probability. Flat $100 moneyline bets at a 0.05 edge threshold went 4201-5880 (41.7%) for $-24887 (-2.5% ROI) over 10081 bets; on the post-tuning 2016-2021 slice it was 2512-3557 ($-8227, -1.4% ROI). Totals: model RMSE 4.42 vs line 4.37; over/under bets at a 0.5-run threshold went 6226-5967 (51.1%, $-32380, -2.7% ROI). VERDICT: competent forecaster, no betting edge. Team strength alone does not beat the closing MLB line; the honest use is as a calibrated forecaster, with probable-pitcher adjustments (see pitcher.py) as the plausible path to any future edge."
